@page "/components/field"

<PageTitle>Field — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Field</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    shadcn's newer, more structured form set. <code>Orientation</code> is an attribute rather than
    a class because the recipe keys off it — vertical, horizontal for a checkbox row, or
    responsive, which stacks in a narrow container and turns in a wide one.
</p>
<p class="doc-note">
    That attribute was missing here for months, and the effect was invisible in the way the worst
    bugs are: the vertical classes live in a variant the extractor never read, so every field in
    the library laid itself out as a row and it looked like a design decision.
</p>

